A||N||3||David Gamache||Better Cam and metal timing gears for an 88 4cyc ?||||5||
Z||000000||David Gamache||12-15-2000||11:15 PM||||Does anyone know if a (California)smog legal cam is avaliable for the 88 fiero with a 4cyc. My cam is due to be replaced and I would like to put a better than factory cam if one exist. Also, has anyone tried the aluminum timing gears instead of the nylon stock gears.  i have heard they make metal gears but have not heard if they are better or worst than stock?||||reg||5
Z||000001||PlasticWrapd||12-16-2000||04:16 AM||||Comp cams has a line of cams that are better than stock, but have the ever elusive EO certificate from CARB.  These are known as "Dual Energy", "Pure Energy", and "High Energy."  The characteristics of these cams include smooth idle, Increased torque and HP, better mileage, acceptable emissions, and the retention of ALL stock components, including springs!  <P>I would tend to shy away from aluminium gears.  Aluminium likes wear quickly and crack when hardened.  Perhaps it would be acceptable for the fairly light loads of turning a cam, but I still have my doubts.  Considering the effort involved to change the gear in a Fiero, I would go with a steel gear (does Rodney sell one?).  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bob Englert||12-16-2000||09:11 AM||||I believe Melling and Coynes makes metal (steel?) timing gears for the 2.5L Duke.  The problem is that they are only available for the 84-86 motors. <P>I had the phenolic timing gear on my 85 4cyl replaced at Ed Parks.  They also replaced the crank gear the first time they did it but used a crank gear form a later Duke engine.  The valve timing marks are not the same on the later engines!  Ed thinks that to use the metal timing gear in an 87-88 Duke you will need to replace both the cam gear and the crank gear with 85-86 parts.  You might want to ask Ed when he returns from vacation.<P>I highly recommed the metal timing gear.  I don't notice any more noise, and the metal gear is a lifetime part.  No more sudden gear failures far from home.<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000003||David Gamache||12-18-2000||01:42 PM||||I will definately look in to the comp cams and find out more about the steel gears. I contacted "Auto zone" auto parts and they said they can order steel gears for 30.00$. The parts book shows the same part number for 85-88 fiero's on the nylon gears, so if the metal gears match the nylons and the timing marks align I may be in good shape.  We will see. The engine is already dropped and I have the gears and the cam out. I will hopefully be able to order the parts and put this back together after the holidays. Thanks for the information so far, it has already been quite helpful.||||reg||1
